<%!-- The second thing every page says, after what the product finds.

    It is one partial rather than three sections because the claim has to be
    identical everywhere: a salesperson and an engineer are being sold the same
    integration story, and the moment two pages describe it differently one of
    them is out of date. Only the examples change with the audience. --%>
<h2 class="section-label">Nothing to integrate. Your AI already knows how.</h2>

<div class="ai-band">
  <div>
    <p class="ai-claim">
      Point any assistant at one URL and it knows the whole service — every
      endpoint, every parameter, every price.
    </p>
    <p class="quiet">
      <a href="/llms.txt"><code>llms.txt</code></a> is generated from the live
      service, so what your assistant reads is what you are charged. No SDK to
      install, no client library, no documentation to work through, no ticket
      for an engineer. Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Copilot — anything that can read
      a page and make a request.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="ai-paste">
    <span class="ai-paste-label">The whole setup</span>
    <button class="ai-copy" data-ai-copy>Copy</button>
    <pre><code id="ai-line">Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API and store my token `csf_live_...` to be used. Then run /demo</code></pre>
    <p class="quiet ai-paste-note">
      That is the integration, start to finish.
      <a href="/start">Walk through it →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="ai-points">
  <%= if @audience == :sales do %>
    <div class="ai-point">
      <strong>You never see an API</strong>
      <span>No key to paste, no terminal, no meter to watch. You ask your
      assistant for the people you want; it does the calls.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ai-point">
      <strong>Ask the way you would ask a colleague</strong>
      <span>"Get me the C-suite at these forty companies, checked, as a CSV."
      The file comes back done.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ai-point">
      <strong>Ten commands it already knows</strong>
      <span><code>/room</code> for everyone at a company, <code>/reach</code>
      for a whole funnel, <code>/clean</code> for a list that has gone stale.</span>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <div class="ai-point">
      <strong>No SDK, in any language</strong>
      <span>Plain JSON over HTTPS, one bearer token. There is no client library
      to pin, upgrade, or wait on.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ai-point">
      <strong>Prices your agent can read</strong>
      <span>Every endpoint carries its cost in the same file, so an agent can
      budget a run before it spends anything.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ai-point">
      <strong>One line in your project rules</strong>
      <span>Drop the URL into <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, <code>AGENTS.md</code> or
      Cursor rules and it stays available without being told again.</span>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<script>
// Scoped to this partial so any page can drop it in without also remembering to
// carry a script. The button is written by the markup rather than by script, so
// it is still visible (and the line still selectable) if this never runs.
(function () {
  "use strict";
  var btn = document.querySelector("[data-ai-copy]");
  var line = document.getElementById("ai-line");
  if (!btn || !line) return;
  btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(line.textContent).then(function () {
      btn.textContent = "Copied";
      setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = "Copy"; }, 1600);
    }, function () {
      btn.textContent = "Select it manually";
    });
  });
})();
</script>
